# Docker build context for the Custotal images.
#
# Both Dockerfiles use the repository root as their build context, so this file
# keeps that context small and guarantees that local state and secrets never
# reach an image layer.

# --- Version control, CI and editor state ------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.editorconfig
.vscode
.idea
.cursor
.cursorrules
*.copilot
.codebuddy
.svn
AGENTS.md
CODEBUDDY.md
openspec

# --- Dependencies (resolved inside the image) --------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Build output and caches -------------------------------------------------
dist
**/dist
.vite
**/.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
# Prisma's generated client is produced inside the image (pnpm db:generate);
# a locally generated copy must not be uploaded in the build context.
**/src/generated

# --- Tests, reports and local run state --------------------------------------
packages/backend/test
packages/frontend/e2e
packages/frontend/src/test
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.test.ts
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
temp
backups
**/backups
*.log
*.log.*
*.dump

# --- Local environment files and secrets (never baked into an image) ---------
.env
.env.*
*.local

# --- Documentation (not needed to build or run the images) -------------------
# LICENSE and NOTICE are deliberately kept in the context so the shipped images
# can include them (Apache-2.0 §4 requires them with distributed builds).
docs
**/docs
*.md
**/*.md
!README.md

# --- Compose files (not needed inside the images) ----------------------------
Dockerfile*
compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yml
.docker
.dockerignore
.docker-compose

# --- OS metadata -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
